---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
---

<CaseStudyLayout
	title="DevHub: Maximizing Developer Productivity • Case Study"
	breadcrumbs={["VMware", "DevHub", "Lead Designer"]}
>
	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<!-- SECTION 1: HERO & TITLE                               -->
	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<article class="case-section">
		<!-- Eyebrow -->
		<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
			<small class="eyebrow">Tushar Roy // Case Study // DevHub</small>
		</div>

		<!-- Main Title -->
		<h1>Turning Fragmentation into Focus</h1>

		<!-- Lead Paragraph -->
		<div class="max-w-4xl mb-10">
			<p>
				At a company where developers shape the future, their own
				day-to-day experience was fractured. Too many tools, too little
				clarity, and no single place to start.
			</p>
			<p>
				I led the design of <strong>DevHub</strong>, a centralized
				developer command center that gave 20,000+ VMware engineers
				unified access to role-aware tools, automated workflows, and
				curated resources—cutting developer onboarding from weeks to
				days.
			</p>
		</div>

		<!-- Hero Visual -->
		<figure class="m-0 mb-4">
			<div class="media-frame">
				<img
					src="/images-devhub/devhub-before-after.png"
					alt="DevHub Before and After Transformation: from fractured tools to unified command center"
					loading="eager"
				/>
			</div>
			<figcaption>
				DevHub Command Center: transforming a landscape of 20+
				disconnected developer tools into a single role-aware portal.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>

		<!-- Metadata Matrix Box: Role and Timeline Panel -->
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mt-16">
			<div>
				<small class="kicker">role</small>
				<h4>Lead Designer</h4>
				<p>
					User research, IA, UI/UX, design system, and prototyping.
				</p>
				<small class="eyebrow"
					><time>2022 Q1</time> - <time>2023 Q1</time></small
				>
			</div>
			<div>
				<small class="kicker">team &amp; scale</small>
				<h4>Core Squad &amp; Scale</h4>
				<p>
					3 Designers, 8 Developers, 1 PM supporting 20,000+
					developers across global engineering teams.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<small class="kicker">outcome</small>
				<h4>80% Faster Onboarding</h4>
				<p>
					Onboarding reduced from 3 weeks to under 5 days; +40% tool
					engagement; 25% drop in service duplication.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<!-- SECTION 2: CONTEXT & THE CHALLENGE                    -->
	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<article class="case-section">
		<div class="case-grid">
			<!-- Left Column -->
			<div class="case-sidebar">
				<small class="kicker">context</small>
				<h2>
					Disjointed workflows, low visibility, and effort duplication
				</h2>
			</div>

			<!-- Right Column -->
			<div class="case-content">
				<p>
					Over years of rapid expansion, VMware's internal tooling had
					fractured into departmental silos. Engineers wasted hours
					every week hunting down documentation, asking on Slack for
					approved tools, and wading through outdated wikis.
				</p>
				<p>
					Without a central catalog, teams frequently rebuilt tools
					that already existed elsewhere in the organization, creating
					redundant maintenance costs and severe cognitive drag.
				</p>

				<!-- 3 User Cohort Cards -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-8">
					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">DEVELOPERS</small>
						<h4>Finding vs. Coding</h4>
						<p>
							Spent more time navigating tribal knowledge and
							80-page onboarding docs than writing code.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">MANAGERS</small>
						<h4>Blind Spots</h4>
						<p>
							Lacked visibility into team tool adoption, sprint
							velocity, and onboarding health without
							micromanaging.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">SERVICE OWNERS</small>
						<h4>Rampant Duplication</h4>
						<p>
							Internal APIs and tools were continually duplicated
							because no discovery mechanism existed across orgs.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Side by Side: Legacy Before & Pain Point Taxonomy -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 pt-2">
					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/01%20before.png"
								alt="Legacy developer portal before DevHub"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Legacy internal toolscape: disorganized link dumps
							and siloed utility pages.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/53%20pain%20points.png"
								alt="Developer pain point taxonomy and friction synthesis"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Pain point taxonomy: cognitive overload, discovery
							friction, and knowledge fragmentation.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="mt-2">
					Disjointed systems forced developers to rely on Slack lore
					and private browser bookmarks just to perform routine tasks.
				</figcaption>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<!-- SECTION 3: RESEARCH & HEURISTIC AUDIT                 -->
	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<article class="case-section">
		<div class="case-grid">
			<!-- Left Column -->
			<div class="case-sidebar">
				<small class="kicker">research</small>
				<h2>Surfacing friction through heuristic audits and interviews</h2>
			</div>

			<!-- Right Column -->
			<div class="case-content">
				<p>
					I initiated the discovery phase with <strong>12+ in-depth interviews</strong>
					spanning engineers, architects, and managers across business units.
					Concurrently, I executed rigorous heuristic audits across the existing
					internal portal suite.
				</p>

				<!-- Developer Quote Callout -->
				<blockquote>
					<p>
						"I spend more time <em>looking</em> for things than <em>building</em> things."
					</p>
					<small class="eyebrow">— MTS Developer, Cloud Infrastructure Team</small>
				</blockquote>

				<!-- Heuristic Audits Multi-Image Grid -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-4">
					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/21%20heuristics.png"
								alt="Heuristic audit on navigation clarity and mental models"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Audit 01. IA Breakdown — Unpredictable navigation
							structures across tools.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/22%20heuristics.png"
								alt="Heuristic audit on cognitive friction and search"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Audit 02. Search Void — Zero unified indexing or
							contextual suggestions.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/23%20heuristics.png"
								alt="Heuristic audit on visual hierarchy and action triggers"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Audit 03. Visual Noise — Cluttered layouts obscuring
							high-frequency actions.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="mt-2">
					Systematic heuristic evaluation surfaced severe violations of
					recognition vs. recall, consistency, and error prevention.
				</figcaption>

				<!-- Personas and Research Highlights Grid -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 pt-6">
					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/40%20personas.png"
								alt="Developer personas: junior, senior, and lead workflows"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Developer Personas: archetypes from newly hired devs
							to senior architects and tech leads.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/51%20research%20findings.png"
								alt="Synthesized research findings and interview insights"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Research Synthesis: quantifying daily hours lost to
							broken documentation and tooling discovery.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="mt-2">
					Grounded in verified user insights: understanding the exact
					divergence between new hires and veteran developers.
				</figcaption>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<!-- SECTION 4: STRATEGY & ALIGNMENT                       -->
	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<article class="case-section">
		<div class="case-grid">
			<!-- Left Column -->
			<div class="case-sidebar">
				<small class="kicker">strategy</small>
				<h2>Co-creating the solution and staying ahead of sprints</h2>
			</div>

			<!-- Right Column -->
			<div class="case-content">
				<p>
					To align cross-functional partners, I led collaborative
					discovery workshops that produced a shared <strong
						>Experience Canvas</strong
					> and an <strong>Ecosystem Map</strong>. Rather than designing in
					isolation, we co-created a prioritized backlog that ensured design
					remained <strong>two full sprints ahead of engineering</strong>.
				</p>
				<p>
					We structured the information architecture around developer
					intent rather than organizational hierarchy:
				</p>

				<!-- Intent Pillars -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-8">
					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">INTENT 01</small>
						<h4>"Start a Project"</h4>
						<p>
							Curated scaffolding toolchains, Git repositories,
							and CI/CD pipelines created in one click.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">INTENT 02</small>
						<h4>"Find a Service"</h4>
						<p>
							Enterprise service portfolio with live health
							status, owners, and documentation.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">INTENT 03</small>
						<h4>"Adopt Best Practices"</h4>
						<p>
							Role-aware tool recommendations, golden paths, and
							compliance checklists.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Full Width Ecosystem Map -->
				<figure class="m-0 pt-2">
					<div class="media-frame">
						<img
							src="/images-devhub/dh-5-workshops.avif"
							alt="DevHub developer ecosystem map connecting roles, tools, and services"
						/>
					</div>
					<figcaption>
						Developer Ecosystem Map: mapping relational dependencies
						between developer personas, internal microservices, and
						cloud infrastructure.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<!-- Side by Side: Experience Canvas & Strategy Backlog -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 pt-6">
					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/11%20alignment%20-%20experience%20canvas.png"
								alt="Experience canvas created during stakeholder alignment"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Experience Canvas: defining core user goals, success
							metrics, and architectural constraints.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/dh-8-strategy.avif"
								alt="Prioritized product backlog and engineering release roadmap"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Roadmap Strategy: establishing a phased rollout that
							kept design two sprints ahead of engineering.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="mt-2">
					Translating high-level strategic alignment directly into
					actionable, sprint-ready product requirements.
				</figcaption>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<!-- SECTION 5: IDEATION & TACTILE PROTOTYPING             -->
	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<article class="case-section">
		<div class="case-grid">
			<!-- Left Column -->
			<div class="case-sidebar">
				<small class="kicker">iteration</small>
				<h2>Rapid paper sketching and tactile prototyping</h2>
			</div>

			<!-- Right Column -->
			<div class="case-content">
				<p>
					To quickly evaluate competing layouts without anchoring
					prematurely on high-fidelity aesthetics, I conducted rapid
					paper sketching workshops with developers. We explored
					modular dashboard widgets, quick-action drawers, and project
					drilldown models.
				</p>

				<!-- 4-Grid of Sketches -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/91%20sketch.jpg"
								alt="Paper sketch: configuring modular widgets"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							01. Widget Configuration — Rapid exploration of
							customizable developer cards.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/92%20sketch.jpg"
								alt="Paper sketch: widget catalog selection"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							02. Widget Discovery — Evaluating how developers
							browse and pin new workspace modules.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/93%20sketch.jpg"
								alt="Paper sketch: responsive dashboard grid layout"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							03. Dashboard Matrix — Testing flexible column
							densities for complex telemetry.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/94%20sketch.jpg"
								alt="Paper sketch: project detail drilldown"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							04. Project Deep Dive — Transitioning from global
							overview into granular repository telemetry.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="mt-2">
					Tactile paper ideation enabled real-time validation of
					interaction ergonomics with practicing software engineers.
				</figcaption>

				<!-- Low-Fi Wireframing & Usability Testing -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 pt-6">
					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/102%20low%20fi.png"
								alt="Low-fidelity wireframe testing of command center layout"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Low-Fi Wireframing: validating the information
							hierarchy and spatial rhythm of widget containers.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/112%20testing.png"
								alt="Usability testing observations and task completion logging"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Usability Testing: timing engineer task completion
							across prototype iterations.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="mt-2">
					Iterative testing revealed that engineers strongly favored
					role-tailored presets over blank, completely unconfigured
					canvases.
				</figcaption>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<!-- SECTION 6: DESIGN - THE COMMAND CENTER                -->
	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<article class="case-section">
		<div class="case-grid">
			<!-- Left Column -->
			<div class="case-sidebar">
				<small class="kicker">design</small>
				<h2>The developer command center</h2>
			</div>

			<!-- Right Column -->
			<div class="case-content">
				<p>
					The final DevHub architecture centers on four core
					interactive capabilities designed to accelerate engineering
					flow states:
				</p>

				<!-- 4 Core Capabilities Cards -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 my-8">
					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">EFFICIENCY</small>
						<h4>Role-Based Personalization</h4>
						<p>
							Dynamic UI adapts to the engineer's team and domain,
							surfacing relevant CI builds, PR reviews, and tools.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">VELOCITY</small>
						<h4>1-Click Quick Actions</h4>
						<p>
							Common workflows—spawning cloud sandboxes, repo
							creation, and pipeline setup—accessible instantly.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">ONBOARDING</small>
						<h4>Smart Toolchain Bundles</h4>
						<p>
							Pre-configured development stacks that get new
							engineers committed to production within days.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="card">
						<small class="eyebrow">CUSTOMIZATION</small>
						<h4>Modular Widgets</h4>
						<p>
							Engineers can pin, rearrange, and configure custom
							telemetry widgets for their active projects.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Full Dashboard Hero Visual -->
				<figure class="m-0 pt-2">
					<div class="media-frame">
						<img
							src="/images-devhub/dashboard.png"
							alt="DevHub unified command center dashboard interface"
						/>
					</div>
					<figcaption>
						The Unified Command Center: aggregating role-based
						tooling, recent commits, CI status, and quick actions
						into one focused view.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<!-- 4-Grid of Specific UI Innovations -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-6">
					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/dh-11-quickactions.avif"
								alt="1-Click quick actions menu interface"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Quick Actions: high-frequency administrative tasks
							executable without page navigations.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/dh-12-onboarding.avif"
								alt="Smart onboarding toolchain interface"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Smart Onboarding: structured guided checklists
							replacing obsolete 80-page onboarding manuals.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/dh-13-recommendations.avif"
								alt="Role-based recommendations and pinned resources"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Personalized Recommendations: intelligent tool
							suggestions based on project assignments.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/131%20vd%20dashboard%20widgets.png"
								alt="Modular widget component library"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Widget Architecture: a scalable design system
							enabling internal teams to author custom widgets.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="mt-2">
					A modular, extensible platform combining speed, role-aware
					customization, and enterprise consistency.
				</figcaption>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<!-- SECTION 7: SERVICE DISCOVERY & JOURNEYS               -->
	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<article class="case-section">
		<div class="case-grid">
			<!-- Left Column -->
			<div class="case-sidebar">
				<small class="kicker">system</small>
				<h2>A living service portfolio and guided journeys</h2>
			</div>

			<!-- Right Column -->
			<div class="case-content">
				<p>
					To combat rampant service duplication, DevHub introduced a
					centralized <strong>Service Portfolio</strong>. Teams
					register their internal APIs, libraries, and microservices
					with live health metrics, DRI contact info, and usage
					documentation.
				</p>
				<p>
					Now, before embarking on building a new service, engineers
					can search, inspect, and reuse existing internal tools with
					zero friction.
				</p>

				<!-- 3-Step Service Portfolio Exploration -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-4">
					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/Day%201%20-%20Service%20Portfolio%20Home.png"
								alt="Service portfolio home catalog"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							01. Portfolio Catalog — Searchable directory of
							internal microservices with status tags.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/Day%201%20-%20Service%201.1.png"
								alt="Service detail page showing health, documentation, and dependencies"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							02. Service Deep Dive — Real-time telemetry, API
							endpoints, and maintainer contacts.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/Day%201%20-%20Service%20Details%201.1.png"
								alt="Service configuration and integration details"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							03. Integration Specs — Instant code snippets and
							client libraries for immediate adoption.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="mt-2">
					Eliminating duplicate work: moving from siloed repositories
					to an organization-wide discoverable service catalog.
				</figcaption>

				<!-- Proposed User Journey Mapping Visual -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 pt-6">
					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/81%20proposed%20user%20journey.png"
								alt="Proposed developer onboarding user journey"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Journey Map 01: The onboarding pathway from Day 1 to
							first production commit.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>

					<figure class="m-0">
						<div class="media-frame">
							<img
								src="/images-devhub/82%20proposed%20user%20journey.png"
								alt="Proposed continuous development user journey"
							/>
						</div>
						<figcaption>
							Journey Map 02: Daily flow state mapping routine
							triage, builds, and peer reviews.
						</figcaption>
					</figure>
				</div>
				<figcaption class="mt-2">
					End-to-end journey maps ensuring every touchpoint reinforces
					developer velocity and minimizes context switches.
				</figcaption>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>

	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<!-- SECTION 8: ACCESSIBILITY & DESIGN GOVERNANCE          -->
	<!-- ===================================================== -->
	<article class="case-section">
		<div class="case-grid">
			<!-- Left Column -->
			<div class="case-sidebar">
				<small class="kicker">governance</small>
				<h2>Design system handoff and accessibility governance</h2>
			</div>

			<!-- Right Column -->
			<div class="case-content">
				<p>
					Building a tool for 20,000+ engineers demanded rigorous
					adherence to inclusive design standards. I authored
					comprehensive accessibility specifications covering keyboard
					navigation, screen reader focus order, and semantic
					hierarchies.
				</p>

